<h2>Segment 258 &mdash; mutually exclusive qualities</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s258S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w1">&#x27;dod</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w2">na</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w3">mi &#x27;thad par</span> thal, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w4">rnag khrag</span> la sogs pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w5">dngos po</span> gsum po <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w6">&#x27;gal ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w7">phyir</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w8">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w9">chu</span> yin <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w10">min</span> gnyis po de <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s258w11">phan tshun spangs &#x27;gal</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w12">dngos &#x27;gal</span> yin pa&#x27;i phyir</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s258S">And <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w2">if</span> you try to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w1">agree</span> to these absurdities, you are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w3">wrong</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w7">for</span> the quality of being <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w4">pus and blood</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w6">incompatible</span> with the quality of being either one of the other two <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w5">substances</span> mentioned. <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w8">Moreover</span>, the quality of being <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w9">water</span> and the quality of <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s258w10">not</span> being water are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s258w12">directly incompatible</span> in such a way that, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s258w11">if something exists and lacks one of these qualities, it must then possess the other</span>.</span>
</div>
